<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Down to one thing this mod still changes about Alpha Skills' defs, from four.

    Sarg Bjornson fixed three of the original four within a day of being told about them
    (2026-09-21/22): "nudist (active)"'s description no longer talks about caravans (worded
    differently from this mod's own wording, but fixed), "pain-driven (active)" now carries its
    own label (matching this mod's wording exactly), and "frozen" now ships a workBoxIconPath
    (matching this mod's texture path exactly, byte for byte). All three patches were removed
    rather than left in place: PatchOperationReplace and PatchOperationAdd do not check whether
    the target already holds the intended value, so leaving them would have meant silently
    overwriting or duplicating Sarg's own fields forever, with no error to notice it by -
    <success>Always</success> only promises the log stays clean if a target goes MISSING; it says
    nothing about a target that still exists, fixed or not.

    What remains is not a fix at all. Sarg confirmed on 2026-09-21 that the two blindness tiers
    sharing one iconPath and one indicatorString upstream is intentional design on his side. This
    mod keeps its own divergence anyway, as its own choice rather than a claimed defect: hue is
    identity for every other passion in this set, and two passions with different learn-rate
    bonuses (elevated 0.5x/1.5x, sublime 1x/2x) sharing a drawing breaks that rule for these two
    alone. The sublime tier is redirected to a gold-iris variant; Alpha Skills' own presentation
    of the pair is left exactly as Sarg intends it - this mod draws its OWN icon for it, nothing
    upstream is altered in meaning, only which texture this mod's own UI shows for it.

    Dormant and active states are separate operations, each with its own <success>Always</success>,
    so one going missing or being redesigned upstream does not take the other with it.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>/Defs/VSE.Passions.PassionDef[defName="AS_BlindPassion_Sublime"]/iconPath</xpath>
    <value>
      <iconPath>Passions/AS_BlindPassionSublime</iconPath>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>/Defs/VSE.Passions.PassionDef[defName="AS_BlindPassion_Sublime_Active"]/iconPath</xpath>
    <value>
      <iconPath>Passions/AS_BlindPassionSublime_Active</iconPath>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
